  "qa-agent.html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n  <title>Molar QA Agent — Autonomous End-to-End Testing Platform</title>\n  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Molar is the autonomous QA agent that writes end-to-end tests, guards production in real time, and clones third-party APIs — so dev teams never use real cards, emails, or users in tests.\" />\n  <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Molar QA Agent — Autonomous End-to-End Testing Platform\" />\n  <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Point Molar at your app. It authors critical-path tests, runs continuous production checks, and opens fix PRs when regressions land.\" />\n  <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n  <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://molar.it/qa-agent\" />\n  <meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://molar.it/og.png\" />\n  <meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1200\" />\n  <meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"630\" />\n  <meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Molar\" />\n  <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Molar QA Agent — Autonomous End-to-End Testing Platform\" />\n  <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Autonomous QA agent for dev teams. Writes tests, guards production, clones Stripe/email/S3 safely.\" />\n  <meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://molar.it/og.png\" />\n  <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://molar.it/qa-agent\" />\n\n  <script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n  {\n    \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@graph\": [\n      {\n        \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\",\n        \"itemListElement\": [\n          { \"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Molar\", \"item\": \"https://molar.it/\" },\n          { \"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Molar QA Agent\", \"item\": \"https://molar.it/qa-agent\" }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\n        \"@id\": \"https://molar.it/qa-agent#webpage\",\n        \"name\": \"Molar QA Agent\",\n        \"url\": \"https://molar.it/qa-agent\",\n        \"description\": \"Molar QA Agent is an autonomous software testing agent that writes end-to-end tests and guards production for development teams.\",\n        \"isPartOf\": { \"@id\": \"https://molar.it/#website\" },\n        \"about\": { \"@id\": \"https://molar.it/qa-agent#app\" }\n      },\n      {\n        \"@type\": \"SoftwareApplication\",\n        \"@id\": \"https://molar.it/qa-agent#app\",\n        \"name\": \"Molar QA Agent\",\n        \"alternateName\": [\"Molar QA\", \"Molar autonomous QA agent\"],\n        \"applicationCategory\": \"DeveloperApplication\",\n        \"applicationSubCategory\": \"Autonomous QA agent / Continuous testing\",\n        \"operatingSystem\": \"Web\",\n        \"url\": \"https://molar.it/qa-agent\",\n        \"description\": \"Autonomous QA agent that reads your application, writes critical-path end-to-end tests in plain English, guards production on a schedule, and uses stateful clones of third-party services so tests never touch real customers.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n  </script>\n\n  <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\" />\n  <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin />\n  <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=Inter+Tight:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\" />\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\" />\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"waitlist-modal.css\" />\n  <style>\n    .doc-page { padding: 64px 0 96px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }\n    .doc-meta {\n      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px;\n      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px;\n      letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3); margin-bottom: 40px;\n    }\n    .doc-meta .num { color: var(--signal); font-weight: 500; }\n    .doc-meta .rule { flex: 1; height: 1px; background: var(--rule); }\n    .doc-grid {\n      display: grid; grid-template-columns: 240px minmax(0, 1fr);\n      gap: 80px; align-items: start;\n    }\n    .doc-sidebar {\n      position: sticky; top: 96px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 28px;\n      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px;\n      letter-spacing: 0.10em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3);\n    }\n    .doc-side-block { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }\n    .doc-side-label { color: var(--signal); font-weight: 500; }\n    .doc-side-meta { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0.10em; line-height: 1.45; }\n    .doc-toc {\n      display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;\n      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 18px;\n    }\n    .doc-toc a {\n      color: var(--ink-3); text-decoration: none; font-size: 11px;\n      letter-spacing: 0.08em; transition: color 160ms ease; line-height: 1.45;\n    }\n    .doc-toc a:hover { color: var(--signal); }\n    .doc-toc a span { color: var(--ink-3); margin-right: 8px; opacity: 0.65; }\n    .doc-article { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 56px; }\n    .doc-kicker {\n      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 500;\n      letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--signal); margin-bottom: 16px;\n    }\n    .doc-title {\n      font-family: 'Instrument Serif', serif; font-size: clamp(48px, 6.4vw, 88px);\n      line-height: 0.98; letter-spacing: -0.025em; max-width: 14ch;\n    }\n    .doc-title em { font-style: italic; color: var(--signal); }\n    .doc-lede {\n      margin-top: 28px; max-width: 60ch; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-2);\n    }\n    .doc-section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; max-width: 64ch; }\n    .doc-section h2 {\n      font-family: 'Instrument Serif', serif; font-size: clamp(28px, 2.8vw, 36px);\n      line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.018em; font-weight: 400;\n    }\n    .doc-section h2 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--signal); }\n    .doc-section h2 .doc-section-num {\n      display: block; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px;\n      font-style: normal; color: var(--signal); letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n      text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 500;\n    }\n    .doc-section p { font-size: 17.5px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ink-2); text-wrap: pretty; }\n    .doc-section p strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }\n    .doc-section ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2em; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.65; }\n    .doc-section li { margin-bottom: 8px; }\n    .doc-cta {\n      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-top: 8px;\n    }\n    .doc-back {\n      margin-top: 80px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;\n      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.12em;\n      text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3); text-decoration: none;\n    }\n    .doc-back:hover { color: var(--signal); }\n    .doc-back .arrow { transition: transform 200ms ease; display: inline-block; }\n    .doc-back:hover .arrow { transform: translateX(-3px); }\n    @media (max-width: 960px) {\n      .doc-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 40px; }\n      .doc-sidebar { position: static; padding-bottom: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }\n      .doc-toc { border-top: 0; padding-top: 0; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body data-waitlist-surface=\"home\">\n  <div class=\"paper-grain\"></div>\n  <div id=\"nav-root\"></div>\n\n  <main class=\"doc-page\">\n    <div class=\"frame\">\n      <div class=\"doc-meta\">\n        <span class=\"num\">QA Agent</span>\n        <span class=\"rule\"></span>\n        <span>Molar / Product</span>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"doc-grid\">\n        <aside class=\"doc-sidebar\">\n          <div class=\"doc-side-block\">\n            <span class=\"doc-side-label\">Category</span>\n            <span class=\"doc-side-meta\">Autonomous QA agent · Continuous testing</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"doc-side-block\">\n            <span class=\"doc-side-label\">Built for</span>\n            <span class=\"doc-side-meta\">Engineering &amp; platform teams shipping web apps</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"doc-side-block\">\n            <span class=\"doc-side-label\">Setup</span>\n            <span class=\"doc-side-meta\">≈ 60 seconds · npx molar-agent init</span>\n          </div>\n\n          <nav class=\"doc-toc\" aria-label=\"Sections\">\n            <a href=\"#what\"><span>01</span>How Molar checks a browser flow</a>\n            <a href=\"#capabilities\"><span>02</span>What it does</a>\n            <a href=\"#different\"><span>03</span>How it's different</a>\n            <a href=\"#start\"><span>04</span>Get started</a>\n          </nav>\n        </aside>\n\n        <article class=\"doc-article\">\n<section id=\"what\"><h2>Describe the task. Check what the browser does.</h2>\n<p>Molar uses a browser agent to carry out a task on your web app and check the result. A task might be to sign in with a test account, add an item, or confirm that an invited teammate can open a workspace.</p>\n<p>Give the agent a URL, a clear instruction, and the access it needs. The result includes the run status and captured browser steps, so you can see where the task finished or stopped. A blocked login or unfinished action needs attention; it is not a passing test.</p></section>\n<section id=\"capabilities\"><h2>Follow signup, payments, and account access.</h2>\n<p>The page is one part of a test. A checkout can display a confirmation while the account still has no access. An invitation can look sent while the email never arrives.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Browser actions:</strong> use <a href=\"/products/cartographer\">Cartographer</a> to explore an app and carry out a defined task.</li><li><strong>Connected services:</strong> use supported <a href=\"/products/clones\">Clones</a> to create and inspect payment, email, identity, SMS, or storage state in a test environment.</li><li><strong>Failure investigation:</strong> use <a href=\"/products/trace\">Trace</a> to inspect captured steps, screenshots, and requests.</li><li><strong>Release checks:</strong> configure <a href=\"/products/guard\">Guard</a> to run selected scenarios as part of your release process.</li></ul>\n<p>Authenticated tasks need a test account and an environment Molar can reach. Service checks also need the relevant integration configured. Beta setup starts with one specific task and its expected result.</p></section>\n<section id=\"different\"><h2>Keep the tests your team already trusts.</h2>\n<p>A browser agent can help investigate an unfamiliar page or attempt a task described in plain English. A maintained test suite gives you explicit assertions that run repeatedly in CI. Both are useful.</p>\n<p>Keep existing Playwright or Cypress checks while evaluating Molar on a missing flow. For example, keep your checkout tests and use a Molar beta setup to investigate what happens when the payment callback arrives late.</p>\n<p>Generated Playwright export and clean replay are still being validated in beta. A successful browser run does not by itself show that a generated test is ready to add to your repository.</p></section>\n<section id=\"start\"><h2>Start with a page you can inspect.</h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/verify\">public browser checker</a> opens a public URL and checks visible page content without changing the page. No account is needed. For an example involving actions, <a href=\"/examples/autonomous-browser-check\">watch the recorded add-and-remove test</a>.</p>\n<p>To test your own app behind a login, <a href=\"/contact\">discuss your beta setup</a>. Bring the URL, the test account or role, and one concrete success condition, such as “the invited member can open the shared workspace.”</p></section>\n</article>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n\n  <footer>\n    <div class=\"frame foot-inner\">\n      <div>© 2026 Molar Labs · Bengaluru</div>\n      <div style=\"display:flex; gap:24px;\">\n        <a href=\"qa-agent.html\" style=\"color:inherit;text-decoration:none;\">QA Agent</a>\n        <a href=\"docs.html\" style=\"color:inherit;text-decoration:none;\">Docs</a>\n        <a href=\"thesis.html\" style=\"color:inherit;text-decoration:none;\">Thesis</a>\n        <a href=\"mailto:pratik@molar.it\" style=\"color:inherit;text-decoration:none;\">Email</a>\n        <a href=\"https://github.com/pratikranaa/molar-it\" style=\"color:inherit;text-decoration:none;\">GitHub</a>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </footer>\n\n  <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/react@18.3.1/umd/react.production.min.js\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n  <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/react-dom@18.3.1/umd/react-dom.production.min.js\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n  <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/@babel/standalone@7.29.0/babel.min.js\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n  <script src=\"site-config.js\"></script>\n  <script type=\"text/babel\" src=\"nav.jsx\"></script>\n  <script type=\"text/babel\" src=\"nav-boot.jsx\"></script>\n  <script src=\"waitlist-modal.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
